+# Compression and first-action boundary for the supplied native family
+
+**Status:** conditional-support. Completed source-bound calculations and independent saved checks are preserved below. Independent review of this assembled note is recorded separately in its packet; formal audit is deferred. This is a boundary for specified trial spaces and certificate algorithms, not a physical impossibility theorem.
+
+The [sparse first-action frame theorem](NATIVE_SPARSE_FIRST_ACTION_FRAME_NOTE_2026-09-09.md) supplies the exact algebra, signed conventions and conditional model premises. The ORIGINAL family has399 raw/798 real closed columns. DATA has402/804 after the three bare sources are appended. The trial frame remains in ORIGINAL. Poles and balancing weights are the same fixed rational midpoint family throughout, with outward square-root coefficients; they are not silently replaced by unknown exact Gauss nodes or pi. Physical scalar uncertainty and analytic quadrature displacement remain separate.
+
+This note establishes three concrete conclusions within that scope. The original four-pair trial frames fail the optional leakage target for both impurities in all five orbits, with certified diagonal lower bounds. Continuing the fixed compression to12 and24 pairs lowers the reported residual bounds but meets none of the five residual gates. Finally, a saved-scalar proof shows that the existing recursive interval-coefficient method cannot complete through specified fresh-support rows at its unchanged width gate. These conclusions do not assert failure of the exact selected subspaces, a different certificate, or the supplied physical model.
+
+## Completed four-pair action evidence
+
+For an exact ordered isometry V=FC, let A_V=V*H_A V and let
+\[
+L=(H_A V)^*(H_A V)-A_V^2
+  =V^*H_A(1-VV^*)H_A V.
+\]
+Then L is positive semidefinite and the squared operator leakage is \(\|L\|\). Every diagonal lower bound is therefore a lower bound for the squared leakage. The real implementation forms the skew compression T of K_A and uses \(L=G+T^2\), consistently with \(H_A=iK_A\). Its impurity update uses the actual Gram rows; the perturbation is not assumed to commute with Gamma. The parent theorem gives the full signed derivation.
+
+The once-only original four-pair action run completed for all five orbits and both impurities. Its exact saved interval results certify every maximum-diagonal lower bound above \(3/10\), in dimensionless h=1 units. Consequently each of these ten particular trial frames has leakage squared greater than \(3/10\), whereas the optional target was leakage at most \(10^{-6}\), or squared target \(10^{-12}\). The rounded \(3/10\) lower statement is derived from the preserved rational bounds, not a retuned acceptance threshold. General generator scaling multiplies the squared quantities by h².
+
+The independent saved checker reproduced all80 recorded beta/C/action stages with separately authored Fraction/isqrt primitives, covering all five original-four frames and both impurities. It did not regenerate the authenticated principal Gram input. The compact runner supplied with this note does not repeat those80 stages; it checks the immutable result bindings, ten gate values and the rounded rational lower statement.
+
+Execution acceptance and scientific target success are distinct: the source-bound action calculation completed correctly, and every optional leakage target was false. No propagated Gaussian state, node amplitude or alpha followed from this run.
+
+## Compression improves while the residual gate stays false
+
+The fixed pilot selected four pairs. The first continuation restored them and selected only pairs5–12. The next restored12 and selected only pairs13–24. Completed native pivot rows were not replayed as new production work. The ORIGINAL399 half-label family, reconstruction weights2 for poles and1 for insertions, and supplied physical entry radii stayed fixed.
+
+The residual gate was
+\[
+r\le\frac{1}{1062\cdot10^6},
+\]
+and the forward-coordinate squared-radius gate was \(d^2\le1/40000^2\). All five orbits passed the coordinate gate and failed the residual gate at each cap. The following are display approximations to reported residual upper bounds, not new fitted estimates:
+
+| Orbit | Four pairs | Twelve pairs | Twenty-four pairs |
+|---|---:|---:|---:|
+| 0 | 0.28099954 | 0.0013125924 | 0.0000018182711 |
+| 1 | 0.69156806 | 0.0049409513 | 0.000016906853 |
+| 2 | 0.69156806 | 0.0049409513 | 0.000016906853 |
+| 3 | 0.81035030 | 0.0063928858 | 0.000021461816 |
+| 4 | 1.10950236 | 0.013855531 | 0.000096619156 |
+
+The12-pair saved check independently validated40 new histories and271320 coordinates, with342930 predicates. The24-pair saved check validated60 new histories and885780 coordinates, with983426 predicates. The original-four saved check covered20 histories and39900 coordinates. Full-stream structural schema was explicitly reused; these checks do not claim that every original native residual entry was independently regenerated. Forward-coordinate certification is not inverse coefficient-C certification and does not by itself bound action leakage.
+
+The physical compression sequence used5.97+11.97+21.25=39.19 external seconds. This cumulative figure excludes distinct action and saved-check jobs. The four-pair action used3.28 seconds and its saved check2.54 seconds. Twelve and24 saved checks used3.11 and8.05 seconds. The separate fresh-width diagnostic used0.87 seconds. Original external receipts, sampled whole-tree peaks and source identities are retained; no new physical execution occurred in packaging.
+
+## Exact fresh-support obstruction for the retained coefficient algorithm
+
+Let a selected half seed introduce a raw coordinate absent from the union of every earlier beta and Gamma-beta support. Its beta coefficient on that coordinate remains exactly plus or minus one half, because every subtraction term is supported on the old union. A fresh insertion similarly retains coefficient one. A new half label that reuses old raw support does not satisfy this hypothesis.
+
+For a saved positive pivot interval \([L,U]\), a fresh half coefficient has magnitude \(1/(2\sqrt r)\). The image interval width is
+\[
+w=\frac1{2\sqrt L}-\frac1{2\sqrt U}
+ =\frac{U-L}{2\sqrt L\sqrt U(\sqrt U+\sqrt L)}
+ \ge\frac{U-L}{4U\sqrt U}.
+\]
+Replacing \(\sqrt U\) by any certified upper bound B preserves the lower bound \((U-L)/(4UB)\). An insertion doubles it. For the retained192-bit interval arithmetic with \(S=2^{192}\) and integer pivot endpoints l,u, the square-root endpoints are
+\[
+a=\lfloor\sqrt{lS}\rfloor,\qquad b=\lceil\sqrt{uS}\rceil.
+\]
+The forced normalized half-coefficient interval has integer endpoints
+\[
+\left\lfloor\frac{S^2}{2b}\right\rfloor,
+\qquad
+\left\lceil\frac{S^2}{2a}\right\rceil.
+\]
+Negative half coefficients have the same width. If a is zero, the positive-divisor guard fails instead. These are one-coordinate consequences of the actual recurrence and outward primitives; no full coefficient reconstruction is needed.
+
+The once-only saved diagnostic traversed all120 selected rows, found78 fresh-support rows, and recorded53 forced width blockers. The earliest *fresh-support witnesses* occur at one-based pair numbers7,8,8,8,9 in orbits0–4. Each of those witnesses already has the exact-image lower bound above the unchanged coefficient full-width gate \(2^{-39}\). Hence the historical recursive interval method cannot complete through those rows with the same saved pivot enclosures. An earlier reused-support row might fail first; these are not certified first execution failures. No full12- or24-pair C construction was launched by this diagnostic.
+
+This is stronger than a finite working-bit complaint for those saved intervals: the exact image width itself exceeds the gate. Increasing coefficient arithmetic precision alone cannot shrink that image. It is weaker than an intrinsic uncertainty theorem for the physical coefficients: narrower direct Gram information, explicit dependency correlations, or a different frame certificate may avoid the historical saved-r interval range. Neither the gate nor the old source is changed here.
+
+## Evidence, recovery and portable verification
+
+The [packet recovery manifest](../.claude/science/physics-loops/native-compression-action-boundary-20260909/verification/RECOVERY_MANIFEST.json) binds compact original results, ROOT/POST receipts, source reviews and the full fresh-width scalar output. It also records exact Git commit/path/SHA256 retrieval for original large event, history, principal-Gram and source artifacts. Checkpoints62–65 and earlier retained manifests preserve the sequence; the latest retrieval commit is d7d01cbe43766ab34194d6a11c87f54c148a3dec. Original failures and affected source corrections remain in those immutable histories.
+
+The [portable runner](../scripts/native_compression_action_boundary_2026_09_09.py) verifies local hashes and fixed result shapes, exact scalar comparisons already present in the saved certificates, and small independent algebra examples for the fresh-support width identity. It does not execute original coefficient, Gram, compression, action or saved-replay workers. It does not claim full forensic replay completeness from a compact manifest. An independent replay audit must retrieve the indicated original payloads and enforce their source/runtime contracts; a hash or prior PASS is not a substitute for that work.
+
+## No-Go Discipline Gate
+
+N1 — Scope and alternatives. The quantified negative claim is only that the named trial frames fail a fixed target and the named saved-r interval algorithm cannot complete a fixed width gate. The following alternatives remain distinct and open: direct selected-principal certification; sharper scalar certificates; dependency-aware coefficient propagation; a different trial frame; and enlarged action-domain data. None is ruled out here. The actual compression, four-pair action and fresh-scalar tests are recorded as attempted. No five-route exhaustive-impossibility claim or artificial quota-based PASS is made.
+
+N2 — Dependence. Residual failure, inverse-coefficient width failure and action leakage are different predicates. This note does not assert they are independent physical obstructions: the relation between improved input accuracy, changed frames and leakage is unresolved. Coordinate success does not imply any of the other gates. No independent-wall count is claimed.
+
+N3 — Premises. The supplied native Hamiltonian/reference, exact midpoint family, scalar enclosures, ideal-isometry interpretation, signed parent algebra and immutable saved inputs are explicit conditions. The framework axioms do not select this Hamiltonian, law or reference. No additional approved primitive is claimed.
+
+N4 — Matching witnesses. The four-action lower bounds concern only the original four-pair V; the residual outputs concern the fixed4/12/24 compression; the fresh-support proof concerns the specific recursive interval-C algorithm and saved pivots. None is reused as a counterexample to the physical model, a24-pair action result, or another representation.
+
+N5 — Resolution. Per-element checks concern the saved fresh coefficients and ten diagonal lower witnesses. Per-block evidence covers five fixed orbits and two impurities where stated. No independent per-site, full-band per-mode or lattice-wide physical no-go was executed. The paired output records these limits explicitly.
+
+N6 — Partial progress. DATA closure, completed enclosures, coordinate certificates and lower residuals remain useful. The requested final propagation estimate and alpha are absent; their absence is not evidence of impossibility. Candidate selected-principal, sharper-scalar and expanded-domain routes are prospects only, with no completed numerical result imported here.
+
+N7 — Strongest counterargument. A correlation-aware direct principal Gram certificate can avoid recursive dependency widening while representing the same exact selected frame. This possibility defeats any broader coefficient-conditioning no-go; it does not alter the historical algorithm-width witness. Better trial spaces can also change the four-pair leakage result.
+
+N8 — History and reopening. Previous source reviews and exact saved checks are reused with their scopes, not counted as new independent physical runs. Reopen an affected inference on changed family, source, physical input radius or certificate method. Preserve the old outcomes rather than retroactively relabeling them. No law-selection, empirical bridge, alpha or TOE closure is asserted.
